## Boundera Context
Boundera helps software vendors and teams working through FedRAMP or CMMC reduce manual evidence, remediation, POA&M, SSP/KSI/package, assessor-review, NIST 800-171, and continuous-monitoring work. We care about FedRAMP 20x, Low/Moderate readiness, CMMC, NIST 800-171, CUI control evidence, KSIs, SSPs, POA&Ms, evidence traceability, authorization/readiness, GovTech/public-sector cloud, defense industrial base teams, and compliance automation.

## Import Criteria
Return should_import=true only when the person is plausibly relevant to Boundera because their profile or the message thread shows one of these signals:
- They work at or lead a cloud/software/security/GovTech/DIB vendor that may need FedRAMP, CMMC, NIST 800-171, public-sector cloud, compliance automation, authorization/readiness, KSI/SSP/POA&M evidence, CUI control evidence, or continuous monitoring.
- They are a FedRAMP/3PAO assessor, auditor, assessment lead, or compliance reviewer.
- They are a CMMC assessor, C3PAO, RPO, auditor, assessment lead, compliance reviewer, or advisor.
- They are a GRC, FedRAMP, CMMC, cloud-security, vCISO, or compliance advisor who supports vendors/customers through FedRAMP or CMMC.
- They are a channel, reseller, marketplace, systems integrator, alliance, partner, or ecosystem contact who could route or co-sell FedRAMP/CMMC tooling.
- The message thread itself discusses FedRAMP, FedRAMP 20x, CMMC, NIST 800-171, CUI, KSI, SSP, POA&M, ATO, public-sector cloud, government compliance, evidence review, authorization, continuous monitoring, or a clear referral to someone who owns those topics.

Reject recruiters, job seekers, hiring outreach, vendors/agencies selling services to us, generic networking, personal conversations, spam, support-only conversations, and people whose profile/thread has no credible FedRAMP/CMMC/public-sector-cloud/compliance relevance.

## ICP Buckets
For imports, set icp and category to exactly one of:
- CSPs: cloud/software/security/GovTech vendors, founders, executives, security/GRC/compliance/FedRAMP owners, or technical operators who may need FedRAMP readiness or ongoing evidence workflows.
- 3PAOs/Assessors: 3PAO firms, assessors, auditors, assessment leads, compliance reviewers, and people whose role is evaluating CSP evidence.
